---
/* RENDERED FROM lib/privacy.mjs, NOT WRITTEN OUT.
 *
 * See that file for why. The short version: a privacy policy is a factual
 * claim about ourselves, it gets the same standard as a claim about a bag, and
 * the specific failure to design against is not a bad policy today — it is a
 * correct policy left standing after the facts change. Frank has told me both
 * analytics and a backend are coming. So every sentence that depends on their
 * absence asks the flag rather than asserting it.
 *
 * WHAT I GOT WRONG IN THE FIRST DRAFT, since it is the reason this page is
 * built this way. It read: "That is not a policy decision we might quietly
 * reverse — it is a consequence of the site being a set of static files with
 * no server to receive anything." Frank quoted it back at me. It is false.
 * Client-side analytics on a static site is the ordinary case and needs no
 * backend of ours; being static prevents nothing. I had dressed a choice up as
 * a law of physics, which is a more flattering claim than the truth and reads
 * as more trustworthy — the exact move this site exists to object to when
 * luggage brands do it with dimensions.
 *
 * TWO THINGS ARE STILL MISSING and the page says so in place rather than
 * omitting them: the controller's identity and a contact address. GDPR Art. 13
 * requires both. They are one-line fills in lib/privacy.mjs.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {
  activeProcessors,
  analyticsLive,
  backendLive,
  BROWSER_STORAGE,
  CONTACT,
  CONTROLLER,
  weCollect,
} from '../lib/privacy.mjs';

const UPDATED = 'September 2026';
const processors = activeProcessors();
const analytics = analyticsLive();
const backend = backendLive();

const Missing = 'not published yet';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy — Sizer"
  description="What Sizer collects, what our host receives, and what your browser keeps. Written from what the site actually does."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-6">

    <section class="pt-12 pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg text-ink-2">
        {weCollect()
          ? 'What we collect, why, and how to tell us to stop.'
          : 'We don’t collect anything about you. Our host still receives your IP address in order to serve the page, and this explains what happens to it.'}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated {UPDATED}.</p>
    </section>

    {/* THE THING A GENERATED POLICY ALWAYS HAS AND THIS ONE DOESN'T. Stated at
        the top, where it is inconvenient, rather than buried — a reader who
        needs to exercise a right needs it before anything else on the page. */}
    {(!CONTROLLER || !CONTACT) && (
      <aside class="mb-8 max-w-3xl rounded-card border border-rule bg-amber-wash p-4 text-[0.9375rem] text-amber">
        <strong>Incomplete:</strong> this policy does not yet name who is
        responsible for the site, or give you a way to contact them. Both are
        required, and until they are here you have no practical way to exercise
        the rights described below. That is a real gap, not a formality.
      </aside>
    )}

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Who is responsible</h2>
      <dl class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <dt class="w-32 shrink-0 text-muted">Controller</dt>
          <dd class={CONTROLLER ? '' : 'text-amber'}>{CONTROLLER ?? Missing}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <dt class="w-32 shrink-0 text-muted">Contact</dt>
          <dd class={CONTACT ? '' : 'text-amber'}>{CONTACT ?? Missing}</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">What we collect</h2>
      {!weCollect() && (
        <>
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
            Nothing. There is no sign-up, no newsletter, no contact form, and no
            analytics. Nothing on this site sends information about you to us or
            to anyone else.
          </p>
          {/* THE HONEST QUALIFIER, and the reason the first draft of this page
              was rewritten. Saying "we collect nothing" and stopping implies a
              guarantee the architecture does not give. */}
          <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
            This is a choice, not a technical impossibility. Plenty of sites
            with no backend at all still track their visitors, using code that
            runs in your browser and reports elsewhere. We have chosen not to.
            We expect to add analytics at some point; when we do, this page will
            say what it is and what it records <em>before</em> it goes live, and
            the date at the top will change.
          </p>
        </>
      )}
      {weCollect() && (
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          See the table below for everything that processes data about your
          visit, what each one receives, and why.
        </p>
      )}
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">What your browser stores</h2>
      {BROWSER_STORAGE.map((s) => (
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          One value, under the key <code class="rounded bg-surface-2 px-1">{s.key}</code>{' '}
          in {s.kind}: {s.holds.toLowerCase()} {s.why_no_consent} Clearing your
          site data removes it.
        </p>
      ))}
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        We set no cookies. There is no consent banner because there is nothing
        to consent to — not because we decided you would not mind.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">The trip you type in</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        The trip checker runs in your browser. Your flights, fares and bags are
        held in the page's own address so that "copy link" produces something
        that actually works, and the verdicts are computed on your machine from
        data the page already downloaded.
      </p>
      {!backend && (
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
          Today none of that reaches us, because there is no server of ours for
          it to reach. We expect to add server-side features later; if any of
          them receives what you typed, this section will say so and say what
          happens to it.
        </p>
      )}
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        Worth knowing either way: because the trip lives in the URL, anyone you
        send that link to sees the same flights and bags. That is the point of
        it — but it means a link is not private, and where you paste it is your
        call.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Who processes your data</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-card border border-rule">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-[0.9375rem]">
          <thead class="border-b border-rule text-[0.8125rem] text-muted">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 font-medium">Who</th>
              <th class="p-3 font-medium">What they receive</th>
              <th class="p-3 font-medium">Legal basis</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {processors.map((p) => (
              <tr class="border-b border-rule last:border-0 align-top">
                <td class="p-3">
                  {p.link ? (
                    <a href={p.link} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="text-blue hover:text-blue-hover hover:underline underline-offset-2">{p.name} ↗</a>
                  ) : p.name}
                  <span class="block text-[0.8125rem] text-muted">{p.role}</span>
                </td>
                <td class="p-3 text-ink-2">{p.processes}</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-ink-2">{p.basis}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] text-ink-2">
        We do not add anything to those logs, do not read them to build a
        picture of you, and do not sell or share data with anyone. There is no
        advertising on this site and no advertising network embedded in it.
      </p>
      {!analytics && (
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] text-muted">
          No analytics provider appears in that table because none is running.
          A test fails the build if one ever appears in the site without being
          listed here.
        </p>
      )}
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        If you are in the UK or EU, data protection law gives you the right to
        ask what personal data is held about you, to have it corrected or
        erased, to object to processing based on legitimate interests, and to
        complain to your data protection authority — in the UK, the ICO.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        In practice there is very little here to exercise those rights against:
        {' '}{weCollect()
          ? 'see the table above for what is held.'
          : 'we hold no record of you at all, and could not identify you if you asked.'}{' '}
        Requests about the host's own request logs go to that host, since they
        are the ones holding them.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        We do not sell personal information, and do not share it for
        cross-context behavioural advertising, under the CCPA or otherwise.
      </p>
      {!CONTACT && (
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9375rem] text-amber">
          You cannot currently make any of these requests, because no contact
          address is published. Fixing that is the outstanding item on this
          page.
        </p>
      )}
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Children</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        This site is aimed at adults planning travel. It is not directed at
        children, and it collects nothing from anyone, of any age.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        This page is generated from a single file in the site's source that
        records what is actually running. When analytics or server-side
        features are switched on there, this page changes in the same commit —
        it is not a reminder someone has to remember to act on.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</Base>
